From 8b00b4a400d2cb033284ed3da9ed43e8ca693df2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:15:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] Land orchestration patches 01-09 (orch-20261021) with
 the test updates the plan names

Applied in order, unchanged: 01 typed STORAGE_FULL/STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE and no masking
ROLLBACK; 02 a recorded cancel request stops new starts; 03 run_interrupts and a
refunded attempt after a handled Ctrl-C; 04 same-model retries honouring retry-after,
then parking agent nodes; 05 setpriv --pdeathsig lifeline on every spawn and tracked
executor groups; 06 infra codes as environment faults and torn JSONL tails; 07 flow-v3
outages stop with ENV_EXIT, never escalate; 08 call-host single flight; 09
budget.maxTokens, TOKEN_BUDGET and a gateway token cap.

Tests: runtime-agent outage cases now expect same-model retries then a park and a
same-model resume (never escalate, no other model); cancel.test.mjs:699 expects the
question not to be asked after the cancel; three cli-cancel tests are fate-sharing
aware (PDEATHSIG kills the sandbox/CLI with its owner, the grandchild helper is still
reaped through its group); runner.test.mjs registers the infra fault classes.
Engine lineage: these are part of engine version 2 (resumes version 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011geBy7JvDqKuqhDyfmzd1U
